  "goodToKnow": "Der Abteilungsleiter (die Abteilungsleiterin) is a head of department, a typical middle-management title in companies and public administration. Die Abteilung is a department: die Personalabteilung (HR), die Rechtsabteilung (legal). Der Leiter means head or manager, while die Leiter (feminine) is a ladder. German workplaces are often seen as fairly hierarchical, with titles used carefully. Plural: die Abteilungsleiter."
